<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ii Naomasa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1561">1561</a>–<a href="/years/1602">1602</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ii Naomasa was one of the four great generals of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a>, commander of the red-armoured troops of the Ii. Wounded at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara">Sekigahara</a> in 1600, he received the former lands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ishida-mitsunari">Ishida Mitsunari</a> at Sawayama. His family moved the seat to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hikone">Hikone</a> and remained among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogunate</a>'s most trusted houses.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ii-naomasa.jpg" alt="Ii Naomasa" width="320" height="636" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ii_Naomasa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
